{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKBurnside"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.burnside_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.burnside_holds","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L137-L137","doc":"Σ d_λ² = n!. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.syt_counts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.syt_counts","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L135-L135","doc":"The cohort entries: SYT counts indexed by some opaque label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.CohortRSKWitness","kind":"structure","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L131-L137","doc":"A cohort-based RSK bijection witness: a finite list of\n`(name, syt_count)` tuples whose squared sum equals `n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rsk_substrate_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.rsk_substrate_exists","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L115-L121","doc":"The old existential form `∃ dimFn, ∑ dimFn² = n!` is now a *derived* consequence of the\ngenuine identity (instantiate the witness with the concrete `dimSYT`), not the axiom itself.\n`RSK_substrate_proved n : RSKBurnsideHolds n` is by definition `∑ p, (dimSYT p)² = n!`, so\n`⟨dimSYT, RSK_substrate_proved n⟩` is exactly the existential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_axiom","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L110-L113","doc":"Compatibility spelling of `RSK_substrate_proved` under the name this was declared with while it\nwas an axiom.  Retained so no call site has to change; **it is a theorem, not an axiom.**  New\ncode should cite `RSK_substrate_proved`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSK_substrate_proved","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L93-L108","doc":"**The substrate identity, PROVED** (S-RSK-bijection).  The RSK bijection's cardinality\nconsequence for every `n : ℕ`, stated with the **genuine `#SYT` count**\n(`QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideHolds n := ∑_{p ⊢ n} (dimSYT p)² = n!`), not a hollow existential.\n\n**This was an `axiom` until 2026-08-23.**  Its own docstring recorded the exit condition —\n*\"pending … the in-repo RSK proof under construction in `SchenstedInsertion.lean`, this is\nassumed; once either lands it becomes a derived consequence\"*.  That proof landed\n(`QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds`, epic `qou-nrex`), so the assumption is discharged and this is\nnow a theorem.  Nothing downstream carries `RSK_substrate_axiom` in `#print axioms` any more.\n\n(Earlier still, it asserted only `∃ dimFn, ∑ dimFn² = n!`, which is satisfiable for trivial\nreasons and did **not** pin `dimFn` to the SYT count — a vacuity flag from the 2026-06-28\nreview.  `rsk_substrate_exists` recovers that existential form.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.BurnsideFromRSK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.BurnsideFromRSK","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**Bridge theorem**: from the RSK upstream class instance,\nderive the abstract `BurnsideIdentity` predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.n_factorial_eq_sum_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.n_factorial_eq_sum_squares","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The Burnside identity: `n! = Σ_λ (dim λ)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.dim","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The supplied SYT-count function (concrete instances use\n`Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.SYT.card`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RSKBridge.RSKBijection","kind":"class","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RSKBridge.lean#L55-L68","doc":"**`RSKBijection` class** — the conjectural Mathlib upstream:\nthe cardinality consequence of the RSK correspondence.\n\nField `n_factorial_eq_sum_squares` asserts the Burnside\nidentity directly; field `dim` is the supplied SYT-count\nfunction.  The class instance acts as the §3b-cond hook for\ndischarging downstream `BurnsideIdentity` claims. ","signatureChunk":0}]}